From: Airtype downstream
Subject: [PATCH] model : count the bytes of overlapping mapped buffers once in the memory breakdown

With mmap, llama_model::load_tensors wraps the model files in one mapped buffer per buffer type and
file, each spanning from the first to the last tensor of that buffer type, and
llama_model::memory_breakdown reports the size of each window. Where the tensors of two buffer
types interleave in a file, their windows overlap, and the breakdown counts the shared bytes once
per window. On Apple Silicon the Metal device maps the files as well (MTL0_Mapped), so a model with
CPU-resident tensors between offloaded ones reports far more weights than its files hold: Gemma 4
E2B Q8_0, a 4737 MiB file whose per-layer token embeddings stay on the CPU, reports
CPU_Mapped 2788 MiB plus MTL0_Mapped 4722 MiB, 7510 MiB in all. The pages are the same, so a caller
that budgets unified memory from the breakdown charges the weights more than once and refuses
loads that fit.

memory_breakdown now counts each byte of a mapped buffer once, attributing it to the first buffer
type that maps it, by taking the union of the mapped address ranges. Allocated buffers are counted
as before, and so is the no_alloc projection, which sums tensors rather than windows. Backends that
copy the weights into buffers of their own, such as CUDA, map one window per file, so nothing
changes for them.

Upstream report: not yet filed; master as of efe3626b (2026-10-12) still sums the windows.

Validated against llama.cpp b11201 on an Apple M3 Pro (Metal, 36 GB unified memory), through the
breakdown llama_get_memory_breakdown reports for a loaded context:
- Llama 3.2 3B Instruct Q4_K_M, a 2019 MB file with all layers offloaded: its token embeddings stay
  on the CPU while the tied output layer maps the same tensor into the Metal window, and the
  weights came to 323 MB of CPU_Mapped plus 2012 MB of MTL0_Mapped, 2335 MB in all, before the
  patch and no more than the file after it. The airtype-desktop-inference-sidecar-engine test
  llm::tests::gpu::the_weights_on_metal_are_charged_once_for_each_byte_of_the_file checks this.
- Gemma 4 E2B Q8_0, the 4737 MiB file above, fully offloaded with a 4096-token context and its
  projector: the Airtype desktop app measured its loaded footprint at 9.80 GB before the patch,
  over its 9.66 GB unified-memory budget, so it refused to serve the model, and at 6.83 GB after
  it, which it serves.

diff --git a/src/llama-model.cpp b/src/llama-model.cpp
index ab5e744..e4a2cae 100644
--- a/src/llama-model.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-model.cpp
@@ -1204,6 +1204,9 @@ struct llama_model::impl {
     // contexts where the model tensors metadata is stored as well as the corresponding buffers:
     std::vector<std::pair<ggml_context_ptr, std::vector<ggml_backend_buffer_ptr>>> ctxs_bufs;
 
+    // the buffers among ctxs_bufs that map a range of the model files instead of allocating memory
+    std::vector<ggml_backend_buffer_t> mapped_bufs;
+
     buft_list_t cpu_buft_list;
     std::map<ggml_backend_dev_t, buft_list_t> gpu_buft_list;
 
@@ -1860,6 +1863,7 @@ bool llama_model_base::load_tensors(llama_model_loader & ml) {
                 }
                 bufs.emplace_back(buf);
                 buf_map.emplace(idx, buf);
+                pimpl->mapped_bufs.push_back(buf);
             }
         } else {
             ggml_backend_buffer_t buf;
@@ -1997,8 +2001,28 @@ llama_split_mode llama_model::split_mode() const {
     return params.split_mode;
 }
 
+// the number of bytes the address ranges [first, last) cover, each counted once
+static size_t llama_ranges_union_size(std::vector<std::pair<uintptr_t, uintptr_t>> ranges) {
+    std::sort(ranges.begin(), ranges.end());
+    size_t   total   = 0;
+    uintptr_t covered = 0; // the end of the ranges counted so far
+    for (const auto & [first, last] : ranges) {
+        const uintptr_t begin = std::max(first, covered);
+        if (last > begin) {
+            total  += last - begin;
+            covered = last;
+        }
+    }
+    return total;
+}
+
 std::map<ggml_backend_buffer_type_t, size_t> llama_model::memory_breakdown() const {
     std::map<ggml_backend_buffer_type_t, size_t> ret;
+    // each mapped buffer is a window onto the model files, sized to span the tensors of its buffer
+    // type, so the windows of two buffer types overlap wherever their tensors interleave in a file:
+    // with Metal mapping the files as well, the windows of a model can add up to more than the
+    // files themselves; a mapped byte is counted once, for the first buffer type that maps it
+    std::vector<std::pair<uintptr_t, uintptr_t>> mapped_ranges;
     for (const auto & [ctx, bufs] : pimpl->ctxs_bufs) {
         if (hparams.no_alloc) {
             GGML_ASSERT(bufs.size() == 1);
@@ -2009,7 +2033,15 @@ std::map<ggml_backend_buffer_type_t, size_t> llama_model::memory_breakdown() con
         } else {
             for (const auto & buf : bufs) {
                 // GGML_ASSERT(ggml_backend_buffer_get_base(buf.get()) != nullptr); // multi_buffer does not have a defined base
-                ret[ggml_backend_buffer_get_type(buf.get())] += ggml_backend_buffer_get_size(buf.get());
+                size_t size = ggml_backend_buffer_get_size(buf.get());
+                const auto & mapped = pimpl->mapped_bufs;
+                if (std::find(mapped.begin(), mapped.end(), buf.get()) != mapped.end()) {
+                    const size_t    counted = llama_ranges_union_size(mapped_ranges);
+                    const uintptr_t first   = (uintptr_t) ggml_backend_buffer_get_base(buf.get());
+                    mapped_ranges.emplace_back(first, first + size);
+                    size = llama_ranges_union_size(mapped_ranges) - counted;
+                }
+                ret[ggml_backend_buffer_get_type(buf.get())] += size;
             }
         }
     }
